### Toggle Comment Like
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/forum/comment/{{commentId}}/like
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

### Example Response:
# {
#   "success": true,
#   "message": "Comment like toggled successfully",
#   "data": {
#     "id": "comment-uuid",
#     "content": "Comment content",
#     "threadId": "thread-uuid",
#     "authorId": 123,
#     "parentId": null,
#     "createdAt": "2025-10-22T14:27:44.000Z",
#     "updatedAt": "2025-10-22T14:27:44.000Z",
#     "isAnonymous": false,
#     "likeCount": 5,
#     "dislikeCount": 0,
#     "author": {
#       "id": 123,
#       "name": "User Name",
#       "profileImage": "image-url"
#     },
#     "_count": {
#       "replies": 2
#     },
#     "isLiked": true  // <-- This tells the client to show red heart
#   }
# }

### Client-side Usage:
# - When isLiked: true → Show red heart icon
# - When isLiked: false → Show empty heart icon
# - Update the likeCount display accordingly

### Example Usage:
# First click: Like the comment (isLiked: true, likeCount increases)
# Second click: Unlike the comment (isLiked: false, likeCount decreases)
# Third click: Like again (isLiked: true, likeCount increases)

### Notes:
# - Each user can only have one like per comment
# - Clicking again toggles the like state
# - The likeCount will increment/decrement accordingly
# - No request body needed - it's a simple toggle
